---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const description =
  'About Cortex Field Kit, an independent public catalogue for Cortex Domain Consultants.';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description={description}>
  <div class="wrap">
    <header class="page-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>A field catalogue, in public</h1>
      <p>{description}</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>
        Cortex Field Kit is Brenton Swanepoel’s public portfolio and a catalogue of reusable use
        cases and assets for other Cortex Domain Consultants. The work it describes sits around
        Cortex XSIAM, Cortex XDR, Cortex XSOAR, and Cortex Cloud: hunts, correlation and parsing
        ideas, playbooks, lab patterns, and the notes that make them reusable.
      </p>
      <h2>Independence</h2>
      <p>
        Cortex Field Kit is an independent project. It is not affiliated with, endorsed, sponsored,
        or supported by Palo Alto Networks. Names of Palo Alto Networks products are used only so a
        reader can tell which product an entry relates to.
      </p>
      <h2>No customer information</h2>
      <p>
        This repository is public. Entries, issues, and pull requests must not contain customer
        names, data, logs, IP addresses, hostnames, tenant identifiers, or email addresses.
        Documentation addresses from RFC 5737 and RFC 3849, and domains such as example.com, are
        the only sample values that belong here. Seed content is marked with an Example badge so
        it cannot be mistaken for a finished deliverable.
      </p>
      <p>
        Implementation files for a real asset, including content packs and test data, stay in a
        separate private repository. This site publishes the sanitized catalogue entry only.
      </p>
      <h2>How a change ships</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open a GitHub issue with the asset, use-case, or site-feature template.</li>
        <li>When the request is complete, add the <code>agent-ready</code> label.</li>
        <li>A check confirms the required fields and comments that the issue is queued, or names what is missing.</li>
        <li>An agent opens a pull request. Brenton reviews every pull request. Nothing merges unattended.</li>
        <li>After review and merge to <code>main</code>, GitHub Actions publishes the site.</li>
      </ol>
      <h2>Run it locally</h2>
      <p>
        Install dependencies with <code>npm install</code>, then start <code>npm run dev</code>.
        Search is indexed by <code>npm run build</code>. The roadmap stays in its unavailable state
        unless <code>GITHUB_TOKEN</code> is set for the build.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
